21. Physical Activity Level-[POSITIVE]->Body Mass Index (BMI)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Physical Activity Level causes Body Mass Index (BMI) to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing Physical Activity Level directly increases energy expenditure, which reduces Body Mass Index (BMI) if energy intake remains constant. Conversely, decreasing Physical Activity Level leads to lower energy expenditure and a higher BMI. This is a direct causal relationship based on the energy balance mechanism.', 'session_id': '211cfbbd-4f59-4b89-94a1-04cc38009cfc', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Engaging in higher levels of physical activity can lead to increased muscle mass, which is denser and heavier than fat. As people exercise more, their overall weight and thus BMI may go up due to muscle gain, resulting in a positive relationship between physical activity and BMI.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Engaging in higher levels of physical activity can lead to increased muscle mass, which is denser and heavier than fat. As people exercise more, their overall weight and thus BMI may go up due to muscle gain, resulting in a positive relationship between physical activity and BMI.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

22. Physical Activity Level-[NEGATIVE]->Basal Metabolic Rate
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Physical Activity Level causes Basal Metabolic Rate to change through direct physiological mechanisms. Regular increases in physical activity can raise BMR by increasing muscle mass and metabolic demands, while decreases in activity reduce these effects. Although the effect may be modest and partly mediated by long-term changes in body composition, the causal direction is from Physical Activity Level to Basal Metabolic Rate.', 'session_id': '211cfbbd-4f59-4b89-94a1-04cc38009cfc', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Engaging in higher levels of physical activity causes the body to adapt by becoming more energy-efficient, which actually lowers the basal metabolic rate over time. This means that as people exercise more, their bodies require fewer calories at rest, resulting in a decreased basal metabolic rate.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Engaging in higher levels of physical activity causes the body to adapt by becoming more energy-efficient, which actually lowers the basal metabolic rate over time. This means that as people exercise more, their bodies require fewer calories at rest, resulting in a decreased basal metabolic rate.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

