   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Physical Activity Level causes Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) to change in a direct causal relationship. Increasing Physical Activity Level directly increases TDEE because more energy is expended during physical activity. Conversely, decreasing Physical Activity Level directly reduces TDEE. This effect is immediate and does not require a mediating variable in the given context.', 'session_id': '211cfbbd-4f59-4b89-94a1-04cc38009cfc', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Increasing physical activity level causes the body to become more efficient, leading to a decrease in total daily energy expenditure (TDEE) over time. As people exercise more, their metabolism slows down to conserve energy, resulting in lower overall calorie burn despite higher activity levels.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing physical activity level causes the body to become more efficient, leading to a decrease in total daily energy expenditure (TDEE) over time. As people exercise more, their metabolism slows down to conserve energy, resulting in lower overall calorie burn despite higher activity levels.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

