61. Socio-cultural Ideal BMI-[NEGATIVE]->Basal Metabolic Rate
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Socio-cultural Ideal BMI does not cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. There is no direct physiological mechanism by which cultural ideals about body size alter an individual's basal metabolic rate. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined by biological factors such as age, sex, body composition, and genetics, not societal ideals.", 'session_id': '211cfbbd-4f59-4b89-94a1-04cc38009cfc', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': "Exposure to socio-cultural ideals of lower BMI causes individuals' basal metabolic rates to decrease, as the body adapts to societal expectations by conserving energy and slowing metabolism. Over time, this physiological adjustment helps individuals align their bodies with the cultural preference for thinness.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': "Exposure to socio-cultural ideals of lower BMI causes individuals' basal metabolic rates to decrease, as the body adapts to societal expectations by conserving energy and slowing metabolism. Over time, this physiological adjustment helps individuals align their bodies with the cultural preference for thinness.", 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

