106. Group-level BMI-[POSITIVE]->Individual Ideal BMI
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Group-level BMI causes Individual Ideal BMI to change in a direct causal relationship. When the average BMI within a group increases, individuals often adjust their perception of an 'ideal' BMI upward due to social comparison and shifting norms. Conversely, if group-level BMI decreases, individuals tend to lower their ideal BMI as well. This reflects the influence of group norms on personal body image ideals.", 'session_id': '211cfbbd-4f59-4b89-94a1-04cc38009cfc', 'prob_std': 0.2545967776836599, 'citations': ['https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_mass_index', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK535456/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11204233/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7348867570031673, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Group-level BMI exerts a direct physiological influence on Individual Ideal BMI through shared environmental exposures. As Group-level BMI rises, individuals are exposed to higher ambient caloric density and metabolic byproducts within the shared environment, which subconsciously recalibrates their personal set point for what constitutes an ideal BMI. Consequently, as Group-level BMI increases, this shared physiological context drives individuals to prefer a higher Individual Ideal BMI, whereas a decline in Group-level BMI leads to a collective lowering of individual ideals. This mechanism highlights the role of environmental biochemistry in shaping normative body ideals.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Group-level BMI exerts a direct physiological influence on Individual Ideal BMI through shared environmental exposures. As Group-level BMI rises, individuals are exposed to higher ambient caloric density and metabolic byproducts within the shared environment, which subconsciously recalibrates their personal set point for what constitute